From d542a122262c6d7fc361296c435f41b06a6a62f6 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 21 Nov 2026 13:09:42 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] perf(metrics): answer the sync report's run census from kept
 board readers [daveey]

The sync loop's metrics report called active_card_runs every 10 s, which opens
a fresh read-only connection per board and parses each board's schema before
its first statement. On the idle Mac gateway (10 boards) that was the report
step's cost: 0.257 s of CPU over 12 reports in a 120 s window, 2.28 ms per
sync round.

The loop's Reporter now reads the census through the BoardWatch readers the
loop already keeps for outbox_pending, and reuses a board's running rows while
that reader's data_version is unchanged. Pool counts are recomputed each call.
Admission, grant-echo exclusion, owner output and every other collect() caller
keep the fresh per-call read. A board the one-statement read cannot decide, or
that the kept reader cannot open, falls back to active_card_runs.

BoardWatch stores one answer per (path, tag), so the census and the outbox
probe do not evict each other.

10-board Linux fixture, 30 warmed calls: due report 23.5 ms -> 2.2 ms.
---
 hermes_cli/kanban_sync_board_watch.py         |  30 +-
 hermes_cli/kanban_sync_client.py              |   2 +
 hermes_cli/machine_metrics.py                 |  14 +-
 hermes_cli/machine_report_census.py           |  72 +++++
 .../hermes_cli/test_machine_report_census.py  | 277 ++++++++++++++++++
 5 files changed, 384 insertions(+), 11 deletions(-)
 create mode 100644 hermes_cli/machine_report_census.py
 create mode 100644 tests/hermes_cli/test_machine_report_census.py

